fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"valign","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLValign","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLValignO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics\/valign","abstract":[{"text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"text. Defaults are implementation-dependent.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics","title":"MXLDynamics","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Dynamics can be associated either with a note or a general musical direction. To avoid inconsistencies between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and among the letter abbreviations for dynamics (what is sf vs. sfz, standing alone or with a trailing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dynamic that is not always piano), we use the actual letters as the names of these dynamic elements. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other-dynamics element allows other dynamic marks that are not covered here. Dynamics elements may also be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"combined to create marks not covered by a single element, such as sfmp."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normaliz